## RESPONSE ENVELOPE

Every Cloudflare v4 API response uses this standard envelope:

  {
    "success":  true | false,
    "errors":   [{"code": 1000, "message": "...", "documentation_url": "..."}],
    "messages": ["..."],
    "result":   { ... } | [ ... ] | null,
    "result_info": {          // present on paginated list responses
      "page":       1,
      "per_page":   20,
      "count":      1,
      "total_count": 200,
      "cursor":     "..."   // cursor-based pagination (R2, KV)
    }
  }

ALWAYS check success == true before using result.
If success == false, errors[0].code and errors[0].message describe the problem.
All dates are UTC ISO-8601 including microseconds.

### Pagination
  Page-based (DNS, zones, etc.): ?page=1&per_page=50 (max 100 per page usually)
  Cursor-based (R2, KV lists): use result_info.cursor as ?cursor= on the next request
  Continue paginating until result_info.cursor is absent or result is empty.

