## STANDARD WORKFLOWS

### Resolve zone ID for a domain
1. GET /client/v4/zones?name=ry-ops.dev
2. Extract result[0].id → {{CF_ZONE_ID}}
3. Cache for subsequent calls in this session

### Audit DNS records for a zone
1. GET /client/v4/zones?name=<domain> → zone ID
2. GET /client/v4/zones/{{zone_id}}/dns_records?per_page=100
3. Paginate until all records collected
4. Flag: records with proxied: false on A/AAAA/CNAME (potential origin IP exposure)
5. Flag: MX records pointing to unexpected mail servers
6. Report: N records | X proxied | Y DNS-only | warnings

### Deploy a Worker via API
1. Confirm: "Confirm: deploy worker {name} to account {account_id}. Proceed?"
2. Build multipart form:
   - metadata part: JSON with main_module, compatibility_date, bindings
   - script part: bundled Worker JS/TS
3. PUT /client/v4/accounts/{{CF_ACCOUNT_ID}}/workers/scripts/{{name}}
4. Verify: GET /client/v4/accounts/{{CF_ACCOUNT_ID}}/workers/scripts/{{name}}
5. If routes needed: POST /client/v4/zones/{{CF_ZONE_ID}}/workers/routes

### Create a KV namespace and bind to a Worker
1. POST /client/v4/accounts/{{CF_ACCOUNT_ID}}/storage/kv/namespaces
   body: {"title": "fabric-state"}
2. Note returned namespace_id
3. Update Worker metadata to include KV binding:
   {"type": "kv_namespace", "name": "FABRIC_STATE", "namespace_id": "<id>"}
4. Re-deploy Worker with updated metadata

### Set up R2 → Queue event notification pipeline
1. Verify R2 bucket exists: GET /r2/buckets/{{bucket}}
2. Verify Queue exists: GET /queues/{{queue_id}}
3. Create event notification rule:
   PUT /event_notifications/r2/{{bucket}}/configuration/queues/{{queue_id}}
   body: {"rules": [{"prefix": "incoming/", "actions": ["PutObject"]}]}
4. Verify consumer Worker is bound to the queue in its bindings
5. Test: upload a file to the bucket prefix → consumer Worker should receive message

### Purge cache after a deployment
1. Resolve zone ID
2. Confirm: "Confirm: purge cache for {domain}. All cached content will be cleared. Proceed?"
3. POST /zones/{{zone_id}}/purge_cache body: {"purge_everything": true}
4. Or purge specific URLs: {"files": ["https://ry-ops.dev/", "https://ry-ops.dev/blog/"]}

### Rotate a DNS record (e.g., updating origin IP)
1. GET /zones/{{zone_id}}/dns_records?type=A&name=<record> → get record_id and current value
2. Show user: "Current: A record {name} → {old_ip}. New value: {new_ip}. Proceed?"
3. PATCH /zones/{{zone_id}}/dns_records/{{record_id}}
   body: {"content": "{{new_ip}}"}
4. Verify: GET the record and confirm content updated

